  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v4.0.0 - Aligned to Feedemy.KeyManagement 4.0.0 (admin and read API surface)\nSchema V2.3.0: KeyAlarms and two endorsement indexes; IKeyAlarmRepository and the operations views' repository members.\n\nBreaking, with schema V2.0.0: a one-way upgrade. Stop every 3.x node, back\nup the database, run DatabaseMigrator, then start the 4.0 nodes. Mixed\n3.x/4.0 fleets are unsupported; going back is a database restore.\n\n- The repositories implement the 4.0 persistence contracts: keyset query\n  methods (the unused paged and load-all reads are gone), key labels (the\n  KeyLabels table), key and version states, the hash-chained audit\n  (Sequence and hash columns, the AuditChainHead row locked FOR UPDATE),\n  and the new idempotency, endorsement request and import job\n  repositories.\n- Timestamps are DateTimeOffset on timestamptz columns, written as UTC\n  whatever offset a caller sent.\n- A connection string with Enlist=false is refused at registration\n  (InvalidOperationException): a change and its audit rows commit in one\n  TransactionScope, which only an enlisting connection joins.\n- The V2.0.0 script runs in one transaction under the migrator's advisory\n  lock, which records the version in the same transaction.\n- Removed: the obsolete UseNpgsqlPersistence builder methods (use\n  WithPostgreSqlMetadata or AddNpgsqlPersistence) and the obsolete\n  AddEntityFrameworkPersistence alias (use AddNpgsqlPersistence).\n\nEarlier releases (full notes: CHANGELOG.md in the repository)\n\nv3.7.0 (not published to NuGet) - DuplicateKeyException on a\nunique-constraint violation, batched active-version reads, the\nrotation-due index aligned to V1.2.0.\n\nv3.6.0 (not published to NuGet) - Batched pending-version reads; unknown\naudit actions read as Unknown.\n\nv3.5.0 - Key endorsement storage (KeyEndorsements table, migration V1.4.0).\n\nv3.3.1 and earlier - dependency maintenance; the 3.0.0 alignment (.NET 10,\nEF Core 10, parameterized SQL).",
